{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2VhZFkWr7qteRbLkSR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`wc` now has a `--json` flag. The test suite passes (4 tests, including 3 new ones), and the changes are uncommitted in the working tree.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`wc/cli.py`**: added `--json`. In JSON mode the tool prints one object like `{\"files\": [{\"path\", \"lines\", \"words\", \"chars\"}, ...], \"total\": {...}}` and skips the per-file text lines and the text `total` line.\n- **Missing files:** the error still goes to stderr and the exit code is 1 in both modes. In JSON mode a missing file is left out of `files`, and it is also left out of `total`, since `total` sums only the files in `files`.\n- **Text mode:** the text path is the same code as before, with only the JSON branch added around it. I did not do a byte-for-byte comparison against the original version; the existing text test checks one case.\n- **`tests/test_cli.py`**: added tests for single-file JSON, multi-file JSON with a missing file (checks stderr, exit code 1, `files` contents and `total`), and the text-mode missing-file exit code.\n\n**Choices I made that you may want to change**\n\n- `total` in JSON mode covers only the files that were read successfully.\n- `total` is always present in JSON mode, including for a single file.\n\n**Housekeeping:** running pytest left `tests/__pycache__/` and `wc/__pycache__/` as untracked files. I did not delete them or commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4886,"cache_read_input_tokens":45537,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4886},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cfc18d85-f621-4ccf-9007-3b5b9